A wider fuzz over 2000 curves (scales `1e-4`…`1e6`, tolerances `1e-5`…`5e-2`) reported **0 bound violations, 0 tolerance violations, 0 cases over 2x uniform**, worst adaptive/uniform ratio `1.000`.

**Naive-approach failures reproduced:** chord-*line* test accepted a chord `~0.89` off at `tol=0.1`; plain segment-hull test needed `8` segments vs uniform `2` (bound `0.60` vs true `0.028`), now `2`; at `|x|~1e13, tol=1e-12` the resolution-blind version never terminates, while this version returns a bounded polyline flagged `belowResolution:true` with `resolution≈2.22e-3`.
